export default [{lucide:'wrench',title:'Mechanical',description:'Responsible for the structural design and maintenance of the robot. This team handles CAD modeling, manufacturing,  assembly, and fluid dynamics and finite element analysis (FEA) simulations. Their scope includes the robot’s frame,  waterproof hulls and enclosures, manipulation systems, and attachment of auxiliary equipment.'},{lucide:'circuit-board',title:'Electrical',description:'Manages the robot\'s "nervous system," focusing on PCB design, power distribution, and hardware-software integration.  They ensure all components receive stable power and that communication lines between electrical components remain  robust and interference-free.'},{lucide:'rotate-3d',title:'Controls',description:'The "brain" of the robot’s movement and perception. Through simulation and testing, this team develops the primary  controller that integrates sensor data, image processing, environmental sensing, and localization. They translate  high-level navigation goals into precise motor outputs to navigate through the water.'},{lucide:'square-terminal',title:'Software',description:'Maintains the core codebase and underlying intelligence of the robot. This includes nearly all system architecture  like Linux and robot computer administration, middleware (software interface) design using tools like ROS2, and human  machine interfaces (UI/UX). They ensure all software modules integrate seamlessly with the hardware and are the  interface through which the Controls team maneuvers the robot.'},{lucide:'microscope',title:'Research',description:'An interdisciplinary link to the scientific community and research faculty focused on environmental research and emerging technologies.  They manage real-world deployments in Lake Tahoe and Bodega Bay and design environmental data collection and processing systems.'},{lucide:'megaphone',title:'Business',description:'Keeps Cyclone RoboSub funded, organized, and visible. This subteam handles corporate sponsorships, budget management,  social media, PR, and travel logistics. It also drives our creative direction—making it a perfect fit for students  passionate about marketing, finance, graphic design, video production, and community outreach. '}];